            <ArticleTitle>Twenty Nail Dystrophy with Pterygium Unguis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>155-156</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 15 year old female developed twenty nail dystrophy I at the age of 7 years, with formation of pterygium. There was no associated skin, mucous membrane, hair or other ectodermal abnormality. It is considered that lichen planus may be responsible for this condition.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
